A||||4||Tone007||Differences between older Iron Duke and newer Tech4?||||1||
Z||000000||Tone007||10-17-2000||02:06 PM||||Hi, <P>I posted a little while ago about the '86 2m4 I just purchased with 28k miles on it, and was wondering about something. I read somewhere (can't recall where) that 84-86 had the standard Iron Duke and the 87-88 4cyl's were a "Tech4" or something to that effect.  My '86 seems to have the Tech4 engine, it is labelled Tech4 and looks slightly different from the older ones.  Is an '86 having this engine normal?  Also, what differences/advantages/disadvantages does the Tech4 have?<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-17-2000||02:20 PM||||The '87-'88 4-cyl. have a DIS (distributorless ignition system).  The older dukes ('84-'86) have a distributor.  <P>I believe they started calling it a "Tech 4" in '86....it has nothing to do with the DIS though.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 10-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||10-17-2000||02:44 PM||||Click on the link for Ogre's Cave at the bottom of the screen and look thru the info he has on the Dukes....||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-17-2000||11:27 PM||||tech 4... yet another label with no relevance. It's looks ok but means nothing.<P>except for minor changes 84-5-6 are all the same. Notes in my cave cover most of the major variations.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||10-18-2000||05:40 PM||||The 88 dukes had the balance shafts in it. It seems much smoother than the older dukes to me. also 84 dukes didn't have roller lifters.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
